.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-MACHINE-APPROVAL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-machine-approval - Set whether machines members add wait for an owner or admin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team machine approval <team> <on|off> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Choose whether machines members add to the team wait for an owner or admin. With on, a new
machine waits until pb team machine approve; with off, it joins right away.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for approval


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team machine approval acme on
  pb team machine approval acme off
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-machine(1)\fP
